rcer !== undefined &&\n                this._props[name] !== undefined &&\n                !this._bound[name]()\n            ) {\n                (this._props[name] as Signal<unknown>)(coercer(next))\n            }\n        }\n\n        // A DOM move (`moveBefore`) keeps the host set up\n        connectedMoveCallback () {}\n\n        disconnectedCallback () {\n            // Snapshot and clear BEFORE running so re-entrant calls are safe\n            // and the array is always empty after this returns (or throws).\n            const fns = this._cleanups\n            this._cleanups = []\n            runAll(fns)\n        }\n    }\n\n    // One accessor per prop. A function value is taken to be a signal\n    // and bound; anything else unbinds and writes the prop.\n    for (const name of Object.keys(propDefs)) {\n        Object.defineProperty(MicrotagElement.prototype, name, {\n            get (this:MicrotagElement) { return this._props[name]() },\n            set (this:MicrotagElement, v:unknown) {\n                if (typeof v === 'function') {\n                    this._bound[name](v as Signal<unknown>)\n                } else {\n                    this._bound[name](undefined)\n                    this._props[name](v)\n                }\n            },\n            configurable: true,\n        })\n    }\n\n    return MicrotagElement\n}\n27:One call in the builder chain: `withProps`, `withRefs`, `withContexts`,\n31:**Prop**:\n32:A named input declared with `withProps`. Inside `setup` it is a signal.\n42:Every host gets a property accessor for each declared prop. Assigning a\n62:- A signal as a component prop is assigned to the host's prop accessor.\n63:- A signal or function as an attribute on a plain element is bound to\n81:kept and its props rebound, never recreated.\n92:pay nothing; the core entry grows only by the prop accessors.\n118:After a signal is assigned to a prop accessor, the host's attribute no\n// .size-limit.js\nexport default [\n    {\n        name: 