{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GuUGszk5CVG5U5L1pxobSu","type":"tool_result","content":"662:    t.equal(inp.value, 'initial', 'initial value bound')\n1609:// Prop accessors on hosts\n1611:test('prop accessor: reading host.<prop> returns the current value', t => {\n1612:    const El = define('test-accessor-read')\n1624:test('prop accessor: assigning a value updates the setup signal', t => {\n1626:    const El = define('test-accessor-write')\n1640:test('prop accessor: assigning a signal makes the prop follow it', t => {\n1642:    const El = define('test-accessor-signal')\n1656:    t.equal(el.label, 'b', 'attribute does not override a bound signal')\n1664:test('prop accessor: pre-upgrade assignments are picked up', t => {\n1665:    const a = document.createElement('test-accessor-pre') as any\n1666:    const b = document.createElement('test-accessor-pre') as any\n1673:    define('test-accessor-pre')\n1894:test('region: a kept host has its props rebound', t => {\n1906:    t.equal(host.label, 'two', 'prop rebound to the new value')\n1997:test('adopt: a bound attribute and a listener work', t => {\n2005:    t.equal(btn.getAttribute('title'), 'b', 'attribute is bound')\n2058:    t.equal(host.n, 2, 'prop bound')\n2062:test('adopt: a host children range is bound; no range is skipped', t => {\n2080:        'content in the range is bound')\n2106:        'sibling still bound')\n\n**Link**:\nOne call in the builder chain: `withProps`, `withRefs`, `withContexts`,\nor `render`. `setup` is the terminal link.\n_Avoid_: step, method (in prose)\n\n**Prop**:\nA named input declared with `withProps`. Inside `setup` it is a signal.\nAn attribute-backed prop is read from the host's HTML attribute of the same\nname; a property-only prop is set from JavaScript only. Every prop also has\na property accessor on the host: assigning a plain value writes the prop,\nand assigning a signal makes the prop read through to that signal. Once a\nsignal is assigned, the attribute is no longer updated and does not\nreflect the current value.\n_Avoid_: attribute (that is the HTML side of a prop), input, option\n\n**Coercer**:\nA function that turns a raw attribute string, or its absence, into a typed\nprop value. The four builtins are `number`, `string`, `boolean`, `json`.\n_Avoid_: parser, validator\n\n**Schema prop**:\nA prop validated by a Standard Schema object rather than a builtin coercer.\nA failed validation yields `undefined`.\n_Avoid_: validated prop, custom prop\n\n**Ref**:\nA child element the component declares with `withRefs` and resolves when\nthe host connects. By default a ref is found by its `data-ref` attribute.\n_Avoid_: query, element ref, handle\n\n**Statics**:\nThe values exposed on a component's class for use outside the browser:\n`TAG`, `refs`, `render`, and `props`.\n_Avoid_: metadata, class properties\n\nchild position its output is wrapped in `<!--[-->` and `<!--]-->`\nmarkers, and so are children passed to a component. A function-valued\n`on<event>` prop is omitted. A page with no reactive holes and no\ncomponent children renders the same bytes as before.\n\nIn the browser, holes bind by position:\n\n- A signal as a component prop is assigned to the host's prop accessor.\n- A signal or function as an attribute on a plain element is bound to\n  that attribute; `false`, `null`, or `undefined` removes it.\n- A signal or function in child position is a **reactive region**.\n- `on<event>` with a function becomes a listener.\n- Anything else is static.\n\n`mount(container, markup)` **adopts** existing children: it walks the\nmarkup against the DOM in document order, binds, and creates no nodes.\nAn empty container gets new nodes. It returns a dispose function that\nstops effects and removes listeners, leaving the DOM in place. Mounting\ntwice on one container throws.\n\nHosts are opaque. Adoption and reconciliation never descend into a\nhost's own markup, only into its marked children range, if any.\n\nWhen a region re-evaluates, its old nodes are morphed toward the new\nmarkup. Keyed children are matched by `key` and moved; unkeyed children\nare matched by position and tag name and patched. A matching host is\nkept and its props rebound, never recreated.\n\nStripping is unchanged. Creating a component whose render link was\nstripped throws an error naming the tag and pointing at `client: true`\nand the build-time keep list. An adoption mismatch on tag name warns in\ndevelopment and leaves that server subtree untouched.\n\n## Trade-offs\n\nApp code gets one state object and no manual DOM work, at the cost of a\nlarger templater subpath. Consumers who do not import `microtags/htm`\npay nothing; the core entry grows only by the prop accessors.\n\nValue updates go straight through signals with no diffing. Only\nstructural changes (conditionals, lists) pay for a morph, and only over\nthe affected region.\n\nChanging the return type of `html` from string to markup is a breaking\nchange. It is acceptable at 0.0.x, and callers convert explicitly.\n\nComment markers add a few bytes to server output where reactivity is\nused, and nothing where it is not.\n\nTreating hosts as opaque keeps reconciliation simple and leaves a\ncomponent's internals to its own setup, but a region cannot patch inside\na host's markup.\n\n## Consequences\n\nADR-004 is relaxed for the templater subpath only. Its size-limit entry\nis raised to the measured result, and the browser build gets its own\nentry so growth stays visible. The core entry stays budgeted as before.\n\nADR-005 still holds: render links are stripped by default. A component\ncreated in the browser, for example as a list item, must be kept with\n`client: true` or the keep list.\n\nAfter a signal is assigned to a prop accessor, the host's attribute no\nlonger tracks the current value. Tests and docs must read the property,\nnot the attribute.\n\nThe package gains a fourth browser build script and a `browser`\ncondition on the `./htm` export. Bundler aliases that point\n`microtags/htm` at source must make the same split.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"20b62115-22e1-4426-a35b-ff7bd0a9ded3","uuid":"3de7fd5d-08d3-4f99-9648-674e221b84e8","timestamp":"2026-10-15T03:57:37.197Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"662:    t.equal(inp.value, 'initial', 'initial value bound')\n1609:// Prop accessors on hosts\n1611:test('prop accessor: reading host.<prop> returns the current value', t => {\n1612:    const El = define('test-accessor-read')\n1624:test('prop accessor: assigning a value updates the setup signal', t => {\n1626:    const El = define('test-accessor-write')\n1640:test('prop accessor: assigning a signal makes the prop follow it', t => {\n1642:    const El = define('test-accessor-signal')\n1656:    t.equal(el.label, 'b', 'attribute does not override a bound signal')\n1664:test('prop accessor: pre-upgrade assignments are picked up', t => {\n1665:    const a = document.createElement('test-accessor-pre') as any\n1666:    const b = document.createElement('test-accessor-pre') as any\n1673:    define('test-accessor-pre')\n1894:test('region: a kept host has its props rebound', t => {\n1906:    t.equal(host.label, 'two', 'prop rebound to the new value')\n1997:test('adopt: a bound attribute and a listener work', t => {\n2005:    t.equal(btn.getAttribute('title'), 'b', 'attribute is bound')\n2058:    t.equal(host.n, 2, 'prop bound')\n2062:test('adopt: a host children range is bound; no range is skipped', t => {\n2080:        'content in the range is bound')\n2106:        'sibling still bound')\n\n**Link**:\nOne call in the builder chain: `withProps`, `withRefs`, `withContexts`,\nor `render`. `setup` is the terminal link.\n_Avoid_: step, method (in prose)\n\n**Prop**:\nA named input declared with `withProps`. Inside `setup` it is a signal.\nAn attribute-backed prop is read from the host's HTML attribute of the same\nname; a property-only prop is set from JavaScript only. Every prop also has\na property accessor on the host: assigning a plain value writes the prop,\nand assigning a signal makes the prop read through to that signal. Once a\nsignal is assigned, the attribute is no longer updated and does not\nreflect the current value.\n_Avoid_: attribute (that is the HTML side of a prop), input, option\n\n**Coercer**:\nA function that turns a raw attribute string, or its absence, into a typed\nprop value. The four builtins are `number`, `string`, `boolean`, `json`.\n_Avoid_: parser, validator\n\n**Schema prop**:\nA prop validated by a Standard Schema object rather than a builtin coercer.\nA failed validation yields `undefined`.\n_Avoid_: validated prop, custom prop\n\n**Ref**:\nA child element the component declares with `withRefs` and resolves when\nthe host connects. By default a ref is found by its `data-ref` attribute.\n_Avoid_: query, element ref, handle\n\n**Statics**:\nThe values exposed on a component's class for use outside the browser:\n`TAG`, `refs`, `render`, and `props`.\n_Avoid_: metadata, class properties\n\nchild position its output is wrapped in `<!--[-->` and `<!--]-->`\nmarkers, and so are children passed to a component. A function-valued\n`on<event>` prop is omitted. A page with no reactive holes and no\ncomponent children renders the same bytes as before.\n\nIn the browser, holes bind by position:\n\n- A signal as a component prop is assigned to the host's prop accessor.\n- A signal or function as an attribute on a plain element is bound to\n  that attribute; `false`, `null`, or `undefined` removes it.\n- A signal or function in child position is a **reactive region**.\n- `on<event>` with a function becomes a listener.\n- Anything else is static.\n\n`mount(container, markup)` **adopts** existing children: it walks the\nmarkup against the DOM in document order, binds, and creates no nodes.\nAn empty container gets new nodes. It returns a dispose function that\nstops effects and removes listeners, leaving the DOM in place. Moun